{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2127","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Mix Mex Max"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array $$$a$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ non-negative integers. However, some elements of $$$a$$$ are missing, and they are represented by $$$−1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We define that the array $$$a$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if and only if the following holds for every $$$1 \\leq i \\leq n-2$$$:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$$$$ \\operatorname{mex}([a_i, a_{i+1}, a_{i+2}]) = \\max([a_i, a_{i+1}, a_{i+2}]) - \\min([a_i, a_{i+1}, a_{i+2}]), $$$$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"where $$$\\operatorname{mex}(b)$$$ denotes the minimum excluded (MEX)$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$ of the integers in $$$b$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have to determine whether you can make $$$a$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" after replacing each $$$-1$$$ in $$$a$$$ with a non-negative integer."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$The minimum excluded (MEX) of a collection of integers $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots, b_k$$$ is defined as the smallest non-negative integer $$$x$$$ which does not occur in the collection $$$b$$$. For example, $$$\\operatorname{mex}([2,2,1])=0$$$ because $$$0$$$ does not belong to the array, and $$$\\operatorname{mex}([0,3,1,2])=4$$$ because $$$0$$$, $$$1$$$, $$$2$$$, and $$$3$$$ appear in the array, but $$$4$$$ does not."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 500$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$3 \\leq n \\leq 100$$$) — the length of $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n$$$ ($$$-1 \\leq a_i \\leq 100$$$) — the elements of $$$a$$$. $$$a_i = -1$$$ denotes that this element is missing."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" if it is possible to make $$$a$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"NO"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" otherwise."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can output the answer in any case (upper or lower). For example, the strings \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yEs"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Yes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", and \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"YES"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" will be recognized as positive responses."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n8\n3\n-1 -1 -1\n5\n1 1 1 1 0\n6\n5 5 1 -1 -1 1\n4\n-1 -1 0 -1\n4\n-1 1 1 -1\n3\n3 3 -1\n5\n0 0 0 0 0\n7\n3 0 1 4 -1 2 3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\nYES\nNO\nNO\nNO\nYES\nYES\nNO\nNO\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, we can put $$$ a_1 = a_2 = a_3 = 1 $$$. Then,"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\operatorname{mex}([a_1, a_2, a_3]) = \\operatorname{mex}([1, 1, 1]) = 0$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\max([a_1, a_2, a_3]) = \\max([1, 1, 1]) = 1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\min([a_1, a_2, a_3]) = \\min([1, 1, 1]) = 1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"And $$$0 = 1 - 1$$$. Thus, the array $$$a$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, none of the elements in $$$a$$$ is missing. And we have"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\operatorname{mex}([a_1, a_2, a_3]) = \\max([a_1, a_2, a_3]) - \\min([a_1, a_2, a_3])$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\operatorname{mex}([a_2, a_3, a_4]) = \\max([a_2, a_3, a_4]) - \\min([a_2, a_3, a_4])$$$, but "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\operatorname{mex}([a_3, a_4, a_5]) \\ne \\max([a_3, a_4, a_5]) - \\min([a_3, a_4, a_5])$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus, the array $$$a$$$ cannot be "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the third test case, none of $$$a_1$$$, $$$a_2$$$, or $$$a_3$$$ is missing. However, "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\operatorname{mex}([a_1, a_2, a_3]) = \\operatorname{mex}([5, 5, 1]) = 0$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\max([a_1, a_2, a_3]) = \\max([5, 5, 1]) = 5$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$\\min([a_1, a_2, a_3]) = \\min([5, 5, 1]) = 1$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"And $$$0\\ne 5 - 1$$$. So the array $$$a$$$ cannot be "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"good"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", no matter how you replace the missing elements."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"2127A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2127/problem/A"}